{#- One filterable value on a record, as a link that filters the listing by it.

Expects:

* param - The facet's URL parameter, eg "jurisdiction"
* value - The value, which is also what a reader reads
* css_class - The class to put on it
* prefix - Hidden text saying what the link does, eg "Show records from"
* listing_page - The BotCentrePage
* evidence_query - The listing's current query, if the reader has one

Clicking adds the value to whatever the reader has already chosen, and clicking
it again takes it off, the same as the box in the filter panel. With no Evidence
Centre page to link to there is nowhere to go, so the value stays plain text.

Whitespace is trimmed at both ends because these sit in comma separated lists.
-#}
{%- set listing = listing_page|default(none) -%}
{%- if listing -%}
<a class="{{ css_class }}" rel="nofollow" href="{{ listing.url }}?{{ facet_query(evidence_query|default(none), param, value) }}"><span class="sr-only">{{ prefix }} </span>{{ value }}</a>
{%- else -%}
<span class="{{ css_class }}">{{ value }}</span>
{%- endif -%}
